  "model_slug": "in770-mitsubishi-city-multi",
  "aliases": [
    "IN770AIRXXSO000",
    "IN770AIR00SO000",
    "IN770AIR00MO000",
    "IN770 Mitsubishi Electric",
    "City Multi BACnet gateway",
    "Mitsubishi AE-200 BACnet gateway",
    "Intesis 700 Series City Multi"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "VRF BACnet gateway (City Multi groups via centralized controller)",
  "applies_to": "Mitsubishi Electric City Multi systems reached through one or two centralized controllers, up to 50 groups each.",
  "summary": "Intesis 700 Series multi-protocol gateway set up for BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP that talks to Mitsubishi Electric City Multi centralized controllers and serves each group as BACnet objects. It publishes gateway-wide commands, a block per group at ((CC# - 1) x 8000) + (G x 100): on/off, mode (indoor, Lossnay and air-to-water variants), fan, vanes, setpoints and limits, ambient temperature, errors, panel-permission locks, sensors, filter and energy consumption, plus optional per-unit error codes.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP",
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Group instance = ((CC# - 1) x 8000) + (G x 100) + offset, CC# = centralized controller 1 or 2, G = group 1-50; controller 1 group 1 is shown (100-132). Global objects add (CC# - 1) x 8000.",
    "Per-unit error codes: ((CC# - 1) x 8000) + IU address + 15000 and + OU address + 15050; address 1 shown (15001, 15051). They are disabled by default and enabled per controller in MAPS.",
    "Three CXGX_Mode_S/_C pairs share a name: offset 0 for indoor units, 1 for Lossnay, 2 for air-to-water units. Two CXGX_FanSpeed_S/_C pairs (offsets 3 and 4) also share a name; the manual does not say which unit kind each serves.",
    "CXGX_Allow_SETPOINT_Panel_c is printed with a lower-case c.",
    "The BACnet table has no read/write column; access is inferred from object type. Consumption is Wh or kWh as set in MAPS."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "700 Series Air Gateway IN770AIR***O000 - Mitsubishi Electric City Multi Systems to Modbus, KNX, BACnet, MQTT and Home Automation - User Manual",
    "doc_number": null,
    "revision_date": "2026-03-16 v1.0.19",
    "url": "https://www.hms-networks.com/docs/default-source/products/intesis/manuals-and-guides---manuals/user-manual-in770mitxxxo000.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Connect the gateway to the City Multi centralized controller(s), pick BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP in Intesis MAPS, load the groups, send the project, then map each group's _C commands and _S status objects from its instance block.",
